SUMMARY:Malhar Barse: Where Clouds Meet Music
DESCRIPTION:The transformative beauty of rain is captured in the sounds of raga Malhar. While the 2009 concert gathered compositions whose lyrics evoked the monsoon’s imagery and mood\, this morning turns inward\, tracing the streams of raga Malhar itself: its many variants\, melodic identities\, and shifting character from the powerful and dramatic to the serene and contemplative. \nThe performance moves through Miyan ki Malhar\, Gaud Malhar\, Megh Malhar\, and others\, each interpreted through khayal\, tarana\, bandish\, and more. The programme also draws on bhajans and semi-classical compositions inspired by rain\, tracing how Malhar’s essence has travelled across genres\, connecting people through the magic of the monsoon: the anticipation before the rain\, the romance of it\, and the particular ache of longing that only this season seems to carry. The ensemble features Mowna Ramachandra on vocals\, Sumit Naik on tabla\, Tejas Katori on harmonium\, and Supreetha Pradeep on tanpura. \nThis performance is part of a series marking twenty years of BIC. It is a chance to trace what has changed\, what has endured\, and how ideas evolve over time. BIC is proud to have been host to conversations that connect culture\, ideas\, and public life across two decades. \nSupported by: \n \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nTwenty Years On: Revisiting Voices from BIC’s Founding Years\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeJgtz0H32vZTNVyJnbuc2PywsX_6lNYiYQkZSfhB3cBZ4Nxw/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Performers*: Mowna Ramachandra\, Sumith Naik\, Tejas Katoti\n*Event Categories*: Culture\, Music\, Performing Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/malhar-barse-where-clouds-meet-music/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Culture,Music,Performing Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Thumbnail_MB.jpg
END:VEVENT
