SUMMARY:Berake Soppu
DESCRIPTION:Language: English and Kannada \nWhat if there is no such thing as a weed? This walking workshop challenges the very notion\, exploring the uses\, benefits\, and precautions of foraging for wild edible greens growing in plain sight around us. \nIn Kannada\, berake soppu refers to a mix of wild greens traditionally foraged by women from fields\, open spaces\, and village commons\, and cooked into nutritious dishes to feed their families. As store-bought greens and ready-made food become more available\, the art of foraging\, the skill of recognising wild edibles\, and the traditional knowledge of cooking with them are slowly disappearing. Every plant has a role to play in its ecosystem\, often one we have simply stopped noticing. \nFollowing a short introduction\, participants will be guided through the neighbourhood to identify wild greens that go beyond the familiar palak\, methi\, or dhantu\, learning their nutritional and traditional uses along the way. The walk closes with tea and further discussion\, situating these plants within their wider social\, cultural\, and ecological significance. Learning to notice the greens underfoot\, the session suggests\, can change the way we see the landscape we move through every day. \nThis programme is part of “Krishna to Kaveri\,” a two-day celebration of Karnataka’s arts and culture taking place over Diwali weekend\, on the seventh and eighth of November. Scheduled ahead of the main festival days\, it offers an early taste of what is to come. \n\n\nDiscovering Wild Edible Greens in our Neighbourhood\nFor Ages 10+\nRSVPs closed. Thank you for your interest.\n \n \n*Facilitators*: Subhashini & Archana\n*Event Categories*: Environment\, Experience\, Krishna to Kaveri\, Sustainability
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/berake-soppu/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Environment,Experience,Krishna to Kaveri,Sustainability
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Thumbnail_berake.jpg
END:VEVENT
